<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the MemosShare app extension.

  An .appex is its own bundle and Apple reads its manifest separately from the host app's, so
  this file declares what THIS bundle's executable can reach, which is a strict subset of the app:

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp — SharedFile.imported() reads
    `.contentModificationDateKey` off the copy it just made of a shared file
    (Packages/MemosShareKit/Sources/MemosShareKit/SharedItem.swift). The copy is staged in this
    extension's own temporary directory, so the reason is C617.1; the timestamp reaches the
    server as an upload's `last_modified`, which rules out DDA9.1.

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults — declared for what this bundle CARRIES rather than
    for what it calls. The extension asks for no preference of its own, but MemosOutbox is linked
    into it, and the one use of the API in this project is in there: the outbox's mobile-data
    choice (Packages/MemosOutbox/Sources/MemosOutbox/UploadPreferences.swift). Apple reads each
    bundle's manifest against the executable that bundle holds, so an .appex declares the reasons
    the code inside it earns. 1C8F.1 for the app group's suite the choice is kept in — the group
    this extension is a member of, which is the point of keeping it there — and CA92.1 for the
    fallback to this process's own defaults when that group is unreachable.

  Audited and deliberately NOT declared: the extension links only MemosShareKit and MemosOutbox,
  neither of which reads volume capacity, system uptime or active input modes. The extension
  carries no client, no session and no credential.

  Nothing is collected and nothing is tracked: the extension writes a capture into the app
  group's outbox and returns.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
                <string>1C8F.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
